('lolita','fr','ba8160c551d4c4913bdf0a763e48df469ebf419d14ce9ee62b04e04fde887bc0','Humbert meets the pregnant Dolores at the Schillers’ home, the house reached in the preceding chapter. This is Coalmont’s present scene; Dolores’s accounts of other places are separate narrative levels.','Humbert retrouve Dolores enceinte chez les Schiller, dans la maison atteinte au chapitre précédent. C’est la scène présente de Coalmont ; les récits de Dolores sur d’autres lieux relèvent de niveaux narratifs distincts.'),
('lolita','es','ba8160c551d4c4913bdf0a763e48df469ebf419d14ce9ee62b04e04fde887bc0','Humbert meets the pregnant Dolores at the Schillers’ home, the house reached in the preceding chapter. This is Coalmont’s present scene; Dolores’s accounts of other places are separate narrative levels.','Humbert encuentra a Dolores embarazada en casa de los Schiller, alcanzada en el capítulo anterior. Es la escena presente de Coalmont; los relatos de Dolores sobre otros lugares pertenecen a niveles narrativos distintos.'),
('lolita','en','1a069474d96d32e932cea28a34192d00eab7822f3e767f89ab5762994b197e4c','Exhausted after the muddy detour, Humbert stops in an unnamed Appalachian town, drinks and watches its illuminated signs. Only the Appalachian region is established.','Exhausted after the muddy detour, Humbert stops in an unnamed Appalachian town, drinks and watches its illuminated signs. Only the Appalachian region is established.'),
('lolita','it','1a069474d96d32e932cea28a34192d00eab7822f3e767f89ab5762994b197e4c','Exhausted after the muddy detour, Humbert stops in an unnamed Appalachian town, drinks and watches its illuminated signs. Only the Appalachian region is established.','Esausto dopo la deviazione nel fango, Humbert si ferma in una cittadina anonima degli Appalachi, beve e osserva le insegne luminose. È stabilita soltanto la regione appalachiana.'),
('lolita','fr','1a069474d96d32e932cea28a34192d00eab7822f3e767f89ab5762994b197e4c','Exhausted after the muddy detour, Humbert stops in an unnamed Appalachian town, drinks and watches its illuminated signs. Only the Appalachian region is established.','Épuisé après le détour boueux, Humbert s’arrête dans une ville anonyme des Appalaches, boit et observe les enseignes lumineuses. Seule la région appalachienne est établie.'),
('lolita','es','1a069474d96d32e932cea28a34192d00eab7822f3e767f89ab5762994b197e4c','Exhausted after the muddy detour, Humbert stops in an unnamed Appalachian town, drinks and watches its illuminated signs. Only the Appalachian region is established.','Agotado tras el desvío embarrado, Humbert se detiene en una localidad anónima de los Apalaches, bebe y observa los letreros luminosos. Solo queda establecida la región apalachiana.'),
('lolita','en','189722defb2e89084ce26d4c67e80873423507d70b79b47d3a3cbf12b2ac3242','In the afterword, Nabokov recalls reading the early Russian prototype to friends in wartime Paris. This is an autobiographical scene, separate from Humbert’s fictional journeys.','In the afterword, Nabokov recalls reading the early Russian prototype to friends in wartime Paris. This is an autobiographical scene, separate from Humbert’s fictional journeys.'),
('lolita','it','189722defb2e89084ce26d4c67e80873423507d70b79b47d3a3cbf12b2ac3242','In the afterword, Nabokov recalls reading the early Russian prototype to friends in wartime Paris. This is an autobiographical scene, separate from Humbert’s fictional journeys.','Nella postfazione Nabokov ricorda la lettura del primo prototipo russo agli amici nella Parigi di guerra. È una scena autobiografica, distinta dai viaggi immaginari di Humbert.'),
('lolita','fr','189722defb2e89084ce26d4c67e80873423507d70b79b47d3a3cbf12b2ac3242','In the afterword, Nabokov recalls reading the early Russian prototype to friends in wartime Paris. This is an autobiographical scene, separate from Humbert’s fictional journeys.','Dans la postface, Nabokov se rappelle la lecture du premier prototype russe à des amis dans le Paris de guerre. C’est une scène autobiographique, distincte des voyages fictifs de Humbert.'),
('lolita','es','189722defb2e89084ce26d4c67e80873423507d70b79b47d3a3cbf12b2ac3242','In the afterword, Nabokov recalls reading the early Russian prototype to friends in wartime Paris. This is an autobiographical scene, separate from Humbert’s fictional journeys.','En el epílogo, Nabokov recuerda la lectura del primer prototipo ruso a unos amigos en el París de guerra. Es una escena autobiográfica, distinta de los viajes ficticios de Humbert.'),
('lolita','en','6fbdf2107e623816350192f5c4574597f090557dce57d067bbea9dd15280b9e1','The outline indicates the state established for the narrated scenes, not the position of a court, beach, lake or laboratory. It is an area of geographical reference, not a reconstructed route or a probability distribution.','The outline indicates the state established for the narrated scenes, not the position of a court, beach, lake or laboratory. It is an area of geographical reference, not a reconstructed route or a probability distribution.'),
('lolita','it','6fbdf2107e623816350192f5c4574597f090557dce57d067bbea9dd15280b9e1','The outline indicates the state established for the narrated scenes, not the position of a court, beach, lake or laboratory. It is an area of geographical reference, not a reconstructed route or a probability distribution.','Il contorno indica lo Stato attestato per le scene narrate, non la posizione di un campo, una spiaggia, un lago o un laboratorio. È un ambito geografico di riferimento, non un percorso ricostruito o una distribuzione di probabilità.'),
('lolita','fr','6fbdf2107e623816350192f5c4574597f090557dce57d067bbea9dd15280b9e1','The outline indicates the state established for the narrated scenes, not the position of a court, beach, lake or laboratory. It is an area of geographical reference, not a reconstructed route or a probability distribution.','Le contour indique l’État établi pour les scènes racontées, pas la position d’un court, d’une plage, d’un lac ou d’un laboratoire. C’est un cadre géographique de référence, pas un trajet reconstitué ni une distribution de probabilité.'),
('lolita','es','6fbdf2107e623816350192f5c4574597f090557dce57d067bbea9dd15280b9e1','The outline indicates the state established for the narrated scenes, not the position of a court, beach, lake or laboratory. It is an area of geographical reference, not a reconstructed route or a probability distribution.','El contorno indica el estado documentado para las escenas narradas, no la posición de una pista, playa, lago ni laboratorio. Es un ámbito geográfico de referencia, no un recorrido reconstruido ni una distribución de probabilidad.'),
('lolita','en','d4d0f0508fbf7159a4b4f178a3e727e55203c05708fc2bf51c468901427f5648','US Census 2020 state boundary, generalized to 0.02 degrees. Narrative precision is evaluated separately for each source chapter; internal legacy coordinates do not locate a scene and are not displayed for this outline.','US Census 2020 state boundary, generalized to 0.02 degrees. Narrative precision is evaluated separately for each source chapter; internal legacy coordinates do not locate a scene and are not displayed for this outline.'),
('lolita','it','d4d0f0508fbf7159a4b4f178a3e727e55203c05708fc2bf51c468901427f5648','US Census 2020 state boundary, generalized to 0.02 degrees. Narrative precision is evaluated separately for each source chapter; internal legacy coordinates do not locate a scene and are not displayed for this outline.','Confine statale US Census 2020, generalizzato a 0,02 gradi. La precisione narrativa è valutata separatamente per ogni capitolo; le coordinate interne pregresse non localizzano una scena e non sono mostrate per questo contorno.'),
('lolita','fr','d4d0f0508fbf7159a4b4f178a3e727e55203c05708fc2bf51c468901427f5648','US Census 2020 state boundary, generalized to 0.02 degrees. Narrative precision is evaluated separately for each source chapter; internal legacy coordinates do not locate a scene and are not displayed for this outline.','Limite d’État du US Census 2020, généralisée à 0,02 degré. La précision narrative est évaluée séparément pour chaque chapitre ; les anciennes coordonnées internes ne situent pas une scène et ne sont pas affichées pour ce contour.'),
('lolita','es','d4d0f0508fbf7159a4b4f178a3e727e55203c05708fc2bf51c468901427f5648','US Census 2020 state boundary, generalized to 0.02 degrees. Narrative precision is evaluated separately for each source chapter; internal legacy coordinates do not locate a scene and are not displayed for this outline.','Límite estatal US Census 2020, generalizado a 0,02 grados. La precisión narrativa se evalúa por separado para cada capítulo; las coordenadas internas anteriores no sitúan una escena y no se muestran para este contorno.'),
('lolita','en','2132d9b8c5b47588497dcab3d8e1691a5efd32ebfe4b21f777c32cfced60ed75','<p>Critical geographical sources. Scene classifications also rely on the original chapter context.</p><p><a href="https://journals.openedition.org/ejas/7550" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Monica Manolescu-Oancea, <em>Inventing and naming America: Place and Place Names in Vladimir Nabokov’s Lolita</em>, 2009</a>.</p><p>Dieter E. Zimmer, <em>Lolita, USA</em>: <a href="https://dezimmer.net/LolitaUSA/Trip1.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Trip One</a> · <a href="https://www.dezimmer.net/LolitaUSA/Trip2.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Trip Two</a>.</p>','<p>Critical geographical sources. Scene classifications also rely on the original chapter context.</p><p><a href="https://journals.openedition.org/ejas/7550" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Monica Manolescu-Oancea, <em>Inventing and naming America: Place and Place Names in Vladimir Nabokov’s Lolita</em>, 2009</a>.</p><p>Dieter E. Zimmer, <em>Lolita, USA</em>: <a href="https://dezimmer.net/LolitaUSA/Trip1.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Trip One</a> · <a href="https://www.dezimmer.net/LolitaUSA/Trip2.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Trip Two</a>.</p>'),
('lolita','it','2132d9b8c5b47588497dcab3d8e1691a5efd32ebfe4b21f777c32cfced60ed75','<p>Critical geographical sources. Scene classifications also rely on the original chapter context.</p><p><a href="https://journals.openedition.org/ejas/7550" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Monica Manolescu-Oancea, <em>Inventing and naming America: Place and Place Names in Vladimir Nabokov’s Lolita</em>, 2009</a>.</p><p>Dieter E. Zimmer, <em>Lolita, USA</em>: <a href="https://dezimmer.net/LolitaUSA/Trip1.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Trip One</a> · <a href="https://www.dezimmer.net/LolitaUSA/Trip2.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Trip Two</a>.</p>','<p>Fonti critiche geografiche. Le categorie delle scene si basano anche sul contesto del capitolo originale.</p><p><a href="https://journals.openedition.org/ejas/7550" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Monica Manolescu-Oancea, <em>Inventing and naming America: Place and Place Names in Vladimir Nabokov’s Lolita</em>, 2009</a>.</p><p>Dieter E. Zimmer, <em>Lolita, USA</em>: <a href="https://dezimmer.net/LolitaUSA/Trip1.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Trip One</a> · <a href="https://www.dezimmer.net/LolitaUSA/Trip2.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Trip Two</a>.</p>'),
('lolita','fr','2132d9b8c5b47588497dcab3d8e1691a5efd32ebfe4b21f777c32cfced60ed75','<p>Critical geographical sources. Scene classifications also rely on the original chapter context.</p><p><a href="https://journals.openedition.org/ejas/7550" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Monica Manolescu-Oancea, <em>Inventing and naming America: Place and Place Names in Vladimir Nabokov’s Lolita</em>, 2009</a>.</p><p>Dieter E. Zimmer, <em>Lolita, USA</em>: <a href="https://dezimmer.net/LolitaUSA/Trip1.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Trip One</a> · <a href="https://www.dezimmer.net/LolitaUSA/Trip2.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Trip Two</a>.</p>','<p>Sources critiques géographiques. Les catégories des scènes reposent aussi sur le contexte du chapitre original.</p><p><a href="https://journals.openedition.org/ejas/7550" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Monica Manolescu-Oancea, <em>Inventing and naming America: Place and Place Names in Vladimir Nabokov’s Lolita</em>, 2009</a>.</p><p>Dieter E. Zimmer, <em>Lolita, USA</em>: <a href="https://dezimmer.net/LolitaUSA/Trip1.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Trip One</a> · <a href="https://www.dezimmer.net/LolitaUSA/Trip2.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Trip Two</a>.</p>'),
